Falsifies `inter_process_communication::verification::send_preserves_the_invariant`.

The defect: a sender with nobody to meet joins the receiver queue. The two queues are twins,
their pushes differ by one identifier, and `send` and `receive` are written as mirror images of
each other a few lines apart, which is where this kind of slip lives.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(e.one_queue_invariant())`, on a rendezvous that already
holds a queued sender, where the blocked sender lands on the other queue and both are then
non-empty. Every other proof in this module rests on that invariant, and a later receive would
rendezvous a sender with a sender.

diff --git a/crates/inter_process_communication/src/lib.rs b/crates/inter_process_communication/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/inter_process_communication/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/inter_process_communication/src/lib.rs
@@ -404,7 +404,7 @@ impl<T: Node> Rendezvous<T> {
         } else if let Some(receiver) = self.receivers.pop_front() {
             Send::Rendezvous(receiver, me)
         } else {
-            self.senders.push_back(me);
+            self.receivers.push_back(me);
             Send::Blocked
         }
     }
